# TicketX frontend environment.
#
# Copy to frontend/.env for local development:
#
#     cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
#
# frontend/.env is gitignored. Vite inlines these at BUILD time, not at runtime,
# so a change here needs the dev server restarted (or a rebuild on your host).

# --- Google login (optional) ----------------------------------------------
# Must match GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID in backend/.env. Without it, password login keeps
# working and the Google button stays hidden.
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# --- API base URL ---------------------------------------------------------
# Leave this UNSET for local development. Unset, the app calls /api and Vite
# proxies it to http://127.0.0.1:8000, which is what you want locally.
#
# Set it only when the frontend is served from a different origin than the API
# (a Vercel deployment, for example). In production on Vercel this MUST be the
# absolute API origin, because the catch-all rewrite in vercel.json sends every
# unmatched path - /api/events included - to index.html. A request that returns
# HTML shows up in the UI as "Unexpected token '<'".
#
# There is no trailing slash, and no /api suffix: this is the API origin, and
# api.js appends the path.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-api-host.example.com
